      "notes": "how many times this lands could not be read (\"Magic Damage Per Tick\" lands more than once and the source does not state how many times; the dropped total row does not divide by it evenly, so the count is not derivable); this ability states a per-tick figure, so its damage recurs over time — and damage over time is never part of a burst total (SPECIFICATION §3.8). The source was read: it recurs, and both the source's own arithmetic and its own printed rows put the count at 5. It is still not written, and the reason is not in the source: not the count — the DESTINATION. Capturing a count marks the component as recurring, which moves its whole figure out of the burst total and into the damage-over-time line, and SPECIFICATION §3.8 defines that line as damage \"delivered over the effect's full duration FOLLOWING the combo\". All five gouts land inside the 0.75-second lunge itself, so nothing follows the combo at all. Marking it would show 0 burst damage for an ability that resolves inside one cast. RAISED for the lead rather than decided here. No figure is published rather than one published in the wrong place.",
